by `θ = 2·arctan u₀`, with `u₀` the unique root of `P` in `(9/25, 37/100)` and
`T = (6u₀ + 4)/(1 + 2u₀ − u₀²)`.  Every coordinate is a polynomial of degree `≤ 7` in `u₀`
(`Sqpack/S11Opt/Data.lean`, generated by `scripts/s11opt/gen.py`).  Containment is the
admissibility test `sq_subset_box_iff` (44 inequalities, 11 of them tight); disjointness is the
separating-axis test `disjoint_of_dir` along an edge normal (55 pairs, 14 of them in contact).
Each inequality is an exact polynomial identity modulo `P` plus a sign of the remainder on an
isolating interval of width `10⁻⁴⁰`, checked by the kernel (`hIv`).
-/

namespace SquarePacking.S11Opt

